@slow
Feature: Only the expected port is open on the application target
  The target is the acceptance container itself (127.0.0.1 in its own network namespace).

  Background:
    Given "nmap" is installed
    And the following profile:
      | name     | value     |
      | hostname | 127.0.0.1 |

  Scenario: The application port is reachable
    When I launch an "nmap" attack with:
      """
      nmap -Pn -p 22,80,443,3000,8080 <hostname>
      """
    Then the output should match:
      """
      3000/tcp\s+open
      """

  Scenario: No management or web ports are exposed besides the application
    When I launch an "nmap" attack with:
      """
      nmap -Pn -p 22,80,443,3000,8080 <hostname>
      """
    Then the output should not match:
      """
      (22|80|443|8080)/tcp\s+open
      """
